{% from "macros/ui.njk" import sectionHeading %}

<article class="prose-page">
  <div class="stack">
    {{ sectionHeading("Accessibility", "Accessibility statement", 1, "This site is built to be usable by as many people as possible. Last updated " + (updated | readableDate) + ".") }}
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Conformance target</h2>
    <p>
      The aim is <strong>WCAG 2.2 Level AA</strong>, and Level AAA wherever it is
      achievable without harming clarity - for example, generous colour contrast,
      visible focus on everything, and text that reflows and resizes cleanly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What's in place</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A "skip to main content" link, semantic landmarks, and one clear heading order on every page.</li>
      <li>Visible keyboard focus everywhere, and interactive targets at least 44×44 pixels.</li>
      <li>Full support for dark mode and for the "reduce motion" setting.</li>
      <li>A reader text-size control on articles, and layouts that reflow to 400% zoom.</li>
      <li>Meaningful alternative text on informative images; decorative images are hidden from screen readers.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How it's tested</h2>
    <p>
      Every change is checked automatically before it ships: the axe-core and
      HTML CodeSniffer engines run against every page in both light and dark
      themes, and a Lighthouse accessibility score of 100 is required to merge.
      Automated tools cannot catch everything, so pages are also checked by
      keyboard and with a screen reader.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Known limitations</h2>
    <p>
      This is a living site and the content archive is still being migrated. If
      you find a page that is hard to use, that is a bug I want to fix - please
      tell me.
    </p>
  </section>

  {# TODO(ruth): confirm the contact route / any commitment on response time. #}
  <section>
    <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
    <p>
      If something on this site gets in your way, please
      <a href="/contact/">drop me a line</a> and tell me what happened, what you
      were using, and what you expected. I read everything and I'll do my best to
      put it right.
    </p>
  </section>
</article>
